  deployments = [
      {"app": "Mobile-Payments-DB", "region": "af-south-1"},
      {"app": "Citizen-ID-Archive", "region": "us-east-1"}
  ]

  for d in deployments:
      status = "COMPLIANT" if d["region"] in approved_data_regions else "VIOLATION (Data Sovereignty Breach)"
      print(f"{d['app']:<20} | Region: {d['region']:<12} | {status}")
  ```

### 2. Data Classification
* **Concept:** Labeling and grouping organizational information by sensitivity and business impact (**Public**, **Internal**, **Confidential**, **Restricted / Top Secret**) so security controls (encryption, DLP, access approvals) match the value of the data.
* **Practical Task (Map Data Classification Tiers to Required Technical Controls):**
